# R-052 mutations — 2026-09-25

## Rounds 2-5: scripts/ci/workflowRunsCiRule.ts, each clause disabled alone, against tests/unit/ci/workflowRunsCiRule.test.ts (39 cases) at the round-5 head
The install step is `bun install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts`, which closes install lifecycle
scripts (root, workspace member, trusted dependency) as a class. Package-script hooks are refused by
prefix: every `pre*`/`post*` except the existing `prepare`. R14b narrows that back to
`preci`/`postci` by name, and it goes red on the nested-hook cases. The cases apply every bypass
blind review found to the real ci.yml and package.json:
- if: false on the step or the job, a shell override, CI_SKIP_BUILD;
- an install without --ignore-scripts, an extra step before or after the gate, or checkout swapped;
- a trigger removed, retargeted, path-filtered, or given branches [master, '!master'];
- a quoted continue-on-error, or a decoy job;
- a no-op ci script, or pre/post hooks on ci, type-check, lint, test:unit, build or check:routes;
- an unknown runs-on label.
G0/G1 test run-ci.sh's bash no-bunfig gate.
