## Round 6 (after /review on #525): the concurrency pin and the timeout floor
The rule now also pins `concurrency` exactly and requires `timeout-minutes` to be an integer of at
least 20. Either one could otherwise end the check cancelled rather than red. There are 45 cases. The
clauses from rounds 2-5 are unchanged, and their log above still holds (39 cases then).
